  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 13-layer planar multilayer film on aluminum substrate. Stack sequence from air side: hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, then Al (Rakic-LD) substrate. All 13 film layer thicknesses are design variables with bounds 10-400 nm. Illumination: normal incidence, unpolarized, wavelength range 400-2000 nm. Objectives: maximize absorptance in 400-700 nm band, maximize reflectance in 700-2000 nm band. Use coherent transfer matrix method solver. Material names: hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), Al (Rakic-LD).",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 13-layer planar multilayer film on aluminum substrate. Stack sequence from air side: HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, followed by an Al substrate. Vary all 13 film layer thicknesses between 10 nm and 400 nm. Illuminate at normal incidence with unpolarized light across 400-2000 nm. Maximize average absorptance in the 400-700 nm band and maximize average reflectance in the 700-2000 nm band using the coherent transfer matrix method.",
